## Clusterwide default deny

By default the app creates a `default-deny-all` policy in each namespace listed in `denyByDefault.namespaces`.
Setting `denyByDefault.clusterWide.enabled: true` replaces those with one `CiliumClusterwideNetworkPolicy`,
`default-deny-all-namespaces`, that denies all traffic of every namespace, `kube-system` and `giantswarm` included.
The switch is off by default and is opted into per cluster. It is independent of `denyByDefault.enabled`.

- **Namespace opt-out.** A namespace carrying the label `policy.giantswarm.io/default-deny: "false"` is not covered.
  Namespaces without the label are denied. Do not label `kube-system` or `giantswarm` with it.
- **Clusterwide DNS allow.** `denyByDefault.clusterWide.allowDNS.enabled: true` adds `allow-dns-all-namespaces`,
  an L4-only egress allow to CoreDNS, node-local DNS cache and kube-dns for every covered namespace.
  Enable it in the same change as `clusterWide.enabled`, or give every customer namespace a DNS allow first.
  Otherwise DNS breaks the moment the deny lands.
- **Rollback.** First opt the affected namespace out with the label above. If that is not enough,
  set `denyByDefault.clusterWide.enabled: false`, which restores the per-namespace policies
  as long as `denyByDefault.enabled` is still true.

## Standard allows

Five standard allows are always rendered, one `CiliumClusterwideNetworkPolicy` each. A standard allow applies to the
namespaces carrying its allow label with the value `"true"`. Removing the label removes the namespace from the allow.
A label change takes effect within about a minute.

| Allow label | Policy | Allows |
|---|---|---|
| `policy.giantswarm.io/allow-dns` | `standard-allow-dns` | egress to CoreDNS, node-local DNS cache and kube-dns, L4 only |
| `policy.giantswarm.io/allow-kube-apiserver` | `standard-allow-kube-apiserver` | egress to the `kube-apiserver` entity |
| `policy.giantswarm.io/allow-webhook-ingress` | `standard-allow-webhook-ingress` | ingress from `standardAllows.webhookIngress.fromEntities` on TCP 443, 4443, 8443, 9443 and 10250 |
| `policy.giantswarm.io/allow-ingress-controller` | `standard-allow-ingress-controller` | ingress from `envoy-gateway-system` |
| `policy.giantswarm.io/allow-metrics-scraping` | `standard-allow-metrics-scraping` | ingress from `alloy-metrics` in `kube-system` |

- **Purely additive.** Every standard allow sets `enableDefaultDeny: {ingress: false, egress: false}`, so labelling a
  namespace changes nothing while no deny covers it. Only the denies control default-deny.
- **Webhook ingress source.** The default `[kube-apiserver, remote-node]` works on clusters running the Giant Swarm
  Cilium app. AKS needs `[cluster]`.
- **DNS for every name.** `allow-dns` is an L4 allow, like the clusterwide DNS allow. It widens a namespace's FQDN
  allow-list to every name. Namespaces with FQDN restrictions write their own DNS rule instead of using the label.
- **Same-namespace traffic** is not a standard allow. The namespace owner applies a Same-namespace policy.

